nli's chances near 4%", "Single partisan-sponsored poll showing a closer race"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a solid Republican hold: the state leans heavily Republican, Marty Jackley has out-raised Nikki Gronli by roughly five-to-one with a big cash-on-hand edge, and markets give Gronli only about a 4% chance. The lone poll, from a Democratic sponsor, shows a closer race but carries little weight on its own, so the forecast stays near the combined fundamentals at roughly R+14.", "watch": "Any independent polling or unexpected late spending surge for Gronli could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Open seat: Dusty Johnson (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Dakota's at-large House seat is open this cycle as Dusty Johnson steps aside to run for governor. Republicans nominated Attorney General Marty Jackley, a well-known statewide figure who won his primary easily and has raised about $1.4 million with more than $1 million on hand. Democrat Nikki Gronli has raised roughly $260,000 and trails badly in financial resources.\n\nThe state's partisan lean favors Republicans by about fifteen points, and prediction markets price Jackley as a heavy favorite. A late-August poll from a Democratic firm showed a four-point race, but it is the only public survey and its sponsor suggests caution. The forecast expects Jackley to win comfortably, with Gronli needing a major shift in the environment to compete.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -15.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0242, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0